# Consultations whose provider attribution is NOT established
#
# Enforced by check_consultation_provenance (scripts/lib/consultation-provenance.sh).
# A consultation whose filename names a provider must either carry a provenance
# block written by scripts/consult.sh, or appear here with a reason.
#
# This register is not a loophole. It is the opposite: an artifact whose
# attribution is unknown is allowed to exist and is NOT allowed to look proven.
# Every line below is a claim this repository has stopped making.
#
# ── What happened ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# On 2026-07-31, `jcode run -p openai -m gpt-5.6-sol` was found to return
# plausible reports with exit 0 while the tool's own log recorded the request
# being served by DeepSeek:
#
#     auth: DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
#     endpoint: https://api.deepseek.com
#     prv:OpenRouter|mod:deepseek
#
# The -p/-m flags are discarded whenever [provider] default_provider in
# ~/.jcode/config.toml names an API-key provider; resolution slides to
# OpenRouter and the DEFAULT model serves — which in this repository is the
# builder. So the reviewer of the code was the same provider as its writer.
#
# Streams to api.openai.com, by day, from the tool's logs:
#
#     07-24: 13    07-25: 0     07-26: 8     07-27: 66
#     07-28: 0     07-29: (no log)           07-30: 0     07-31: 0
#
# Nothing in this repository noticed. It surfaced because the owner observed
# that a subscription quota was untouched.
#
# ── format ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# <filename>  —  <why attribution is not established>

42-attempt-sol.md
    Records an attempt rather than a review. 2026-07-25, a day with zero
    streams to api.openai.com. Retained as evidence of the attempt, not as a
    consultation.

55-sol-ratification.md
    Committed 2026-07-26, a day with 8 streams to api.openai.com, so the
    attribution is PLAUSIBLE and remains unproven: no per-artifact evidence was
    recorded at the time and the day's log cannot bind a stream to this file.

66-round2-sol.md
    Same day and same reasoning as 55-sol-ratification.md. Plausible,
    unproven.

107-sol.md
    Committed 2026-07-30 17:16, a day with ZERO streams to api.openai.com. No
    log exists for 07-29, so production on the previous day cannot be excluded
    and this is not a finding that it was misattributed. What can no longer be
    asserted is that it was independent — and this is the security review of
    the S1 sandbox isolation backend, the most consequential in the repository.
    Re-run required before it is cited again. See #135.

127-sol.md
    ESTABLISHED as not independent. Dispatched 2026-07-31 08:07; the log for
    that window records prv:OpenRouter|mod:deepseek and a stream to
    api.deepseek.com. Served by the same provider as the builder whose code it
    reviewed. PR #127 was merged citing it as a cross-provider review; that
    condition was not met. See #135.

127-sol-round2.md
    ESTABLISHED as not independent. Dispatched 2026-07-31 10:01, same evidence
    as 127-sol.md. This is the round that verified the round-1 conditions were
    met, so the verification of the verification is unproven too.

66-round1-kimi.md
    Committed 2026-07-26, before any per-artifact evidence was recorded. Kimi
    is reached by a direct API call with no failover in the path, so the class
    of substitution found on 07-31 cannot apply — but "cannot apply" is an
    argument, not a measurement, and this file carries none.

107-kimi-adoption.md
    Committed 2026-07-30. Names the endpoint and model in its prose, which is
    weaker than a recorded response field but is not nothing. Registered rather
    than back-filled: writing a provenance block after the fact from prose
    would manufacture exactly the appearance of verification this register
    exists to withhold.

107-kimi-architecture.md
    Same as 107-kimi-adoption.md.

